    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW24gc8biRbZDFBtjUqNQvj7t)_\n\nImplements the \"Harmonize the highlight with the accent colors used in different themes\" task from c325001.\n\n- `sp-themes`: new `sp-theme-update-lazy-highlight` (on `sp-after-load-theme-hook`, and re-run by `sp-load-theme` after it disables old themes). The `sp-dark`/`sp-light` themes already set `lazy-highlight` from the `bg-search-lazy` role, so they are left alone. For Lambda, Ef and Doric themes the background is the foreground of `sp-theme-lazy-highlight-source` (default keyword face) blended into the default background (0.32 dark, 0.22 light), foreground is the default one. Uses `sp-theme-blend` from the engine; nothing hardcoded.\n- `sp-org-custom-highlight`: `my-org-inline-comment` now inherits `lazy-highlight` instead of fixed yellow.\n- Docs (`.org`) and tangled `.el` edited together; one ERT test added.\n\n`isearch` is not touched.\n\nNot run: no Emacs in the cloud container, so the tangle was done by hand and the test and the look in each theme are untested.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBU7o9uhKE5qFuntp4)_",
    "changed_files": 6,
    "closed_at": "2026-11-02T14:02:22Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "OWNER",
            "body": "The `tangle` check failed on `sp-org-custom-highlight.el`: the doc has had the `my-org-insert-inline-comment` block since c325001, but the `.el` was never retangled, so my hand-tangle was missing 12 lines. I added that block to the `.el` (pushed). The check should re-run on the new head.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
